Backported from LibreOffice master: https://github.com/LibreOffice/core/commit/66a0927a6832
Adapted: 26.2.6.3 already declares getCombinedHoldCyclesInSeconds(), so the
header hunk only makes calculateCombinedHoldCyclesInSeconds() virtual.

From 66a0927a683290a079cd5ed06ed98ce3c1f03ce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Armin Le Grand (collabora)" <Armin.LeGrand@collabora.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 17:08:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CairoSDPR: Force keeping CairoSurfaceHelper for huge
 PixelData
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If we have a really 'big' pixel-based graphic the cost for creating
the mip-map entries is high. If that is the case, force keeping this
entry alive and not getting flushed by using a large number of
seconds. In that case the local MipMap is more important than the
memory kept allocated for fast repaints.

To detect 'big' graphics, compare to an assumed ScreenSize (may also
be fetched from real screen if needed). To react, create a buffer
residing time of one hour (increase if needed).

NOTE: This will increase MemoryFootPrint if isCairoCompatible
is false by holding the local cairo_surface_t in CairoSurfaceHelper
longer than before.

Change-Id: I1cf726f00d459bc0cb19bb1d202e64e010061426
